responses = [503, 503, 200], then 503 forever

budget   check at bottom   check at top   iterator
     3   Ok(3)             Ok(3)          Ok(3)
     5   Ok(3)             Ok(3)          Ok(3)
     2   Err(2)            Err(2)         Err(2)
     1   Err(1)            Err(1)         Err(1)
     0   Err(1)            Err(0)         Err(0)

Budget 0 is the only row where the columns disagree. With the check
at the bottom the loop is a do...while: one request goes out before
anyone asks whether it was allowed.

Now `attempts == budget` instead of `>=`, against a server that never succeeds:
   budget 3: Err(3)
   budget 0: Err(10000)   <- stopped by the 10_000 cap, not by the budget
attempts is already 1 when it is first compared, so 1 == 0 is the first
of an endless run of false answers.
